# Hunt 1 — Failed SSH Login Attempts

## Purpose

Repeated failed login attempts are a common indicator of brute-force attacks against SSH services.

### Query

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData has "Failed password"
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, RawData
```

### Expected Output

| TimeGenerated | Computer | RawData |
|---------------|----------|---------|
| ... | server01 | Failed password for invalid user admin... |

### Why It Matters

A high volume of failed authentication attempts may indicate password guessing or credential stuffing activity.

---

# Hunt 2 — Top Attacking Source IPs

## Purpose

Identify the IP addresses responsible for the highest number of failed login attempts.

### Query

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData has "Failed password"
| extend SourceIP = extract(@"from ([0-9.]+)", 1, RawData)
| summarize FailedAttempts = count() by SourceIP
| order by FailedAttempts desc
```

### Example Output

| SourceIP | FailedAttempts |
|----------|---------------:|
| 203.0.113.77 | 28 |
| 198.51.100.42 | 14 |

### Why It Matters

Ranking source IPs helps analysts prioritize investigation of the most aggressive attackers.

---

# Hunt 3 — Authentication Activity Over Time

## Purpose

Visualize authentication failures to identify spikes or abnormal activity.

### Query

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData has "Failed password"
| summarize FailedAttempts = count() by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)
| render timechart
```

### Why It Matters

Time-based analysis helps identify attack campaigns, brute-force bursts, and unusual authentication trends.

---

# Hunt 4 — Successful Logins

## Purpose

Review successful SSH logins and compare them with failed authentication attempts.

### Query

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData has "Accepted password"
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, RawData
```

### Why It Matters

A successful login immediately following numerous failures may indicate a compromised account.

---

# Hunt 5 — Authentication Summary by Host

## Purpose

Determine which systems receive the highest number of authentication events.

### Query

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| summarize Events = count() by Computer
| order by Events desc
```

### Example Output

| Computer | Events |
|----------|-------:|
| server01 | 175 |
| server02 | 116 |

### Why It Matters

High authentication activity on a single host may warrant additional investigation.

