# Key Takeaways

- Threat hunting is proactive rather than reactive.
- KQL enables rapid analysis of authentication data.
- Repeated failed logins often indicate brute-force activity.
- Time-based analysis reveals attack patterns.
- Hunting results can be converted into production detection rules.
